      "id": 1,
      "text": "Dover was originally called Canal Dover because it sat along the Ohio and Erie Canal, founded in 1807.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dover%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city officially changed its name to Dover on February 12, 1916.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dover%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Dover Public Library’s Local History Room holds extensive books on Tuscarawas County, including the 1884 Warner & Beers history.",
